==Demographics==
Nakama population is estimated at around 117 millions, with 86 million or about 80% of total population living on [[Seijima Island]]. Majority of population inhabited northern part of Nakama while southern Nakama has lower population density. Nakama mostly consist of Southern [[w:Yamato people|Yamato people]] which makes 87% of its total population with homogenous liguistic and culture. Notable ethnic minorities includes: [[Namiyan People]] (5%), [[Fuuki People]] (4%), Okataian (1%), and Korean (1%). 

Nakama have the pretty much high life expectancy at birth compared to any country in the world: 80.6 years for persons born in the period 2010–2015. The Nakamaese population growth decreased as a result of a post–World War II baby boom followed by a decrease in birth rates which caused more controlable population growth (as for 2017 0.20%). Nakama population projected to be peaked in 2050 with population around 130 millions and later begun to be decreased as the trend of population ageing in east asia.

Nakama population in overall have high living standard with HDI rates .858, some part on Northern part of Nakama have HDI rate over .900 while several location in Nakama, most notable [[Ishitani Prefecture]] know to have several demographic issues with lower living standard of .684 (lowest in Nakama) makes inequity development problem in Nakama which rising since the modernization of [[Kurahashi Shogunate]]. Poverty are uncommon in the northern part compared to the several area in the southern part of Nakama however its still uncommon in overall.

Nakama suffers from a high suicide rate. In 2011, the number of suicides exceeded 23,000 for the twelfth straight year. For now the suicides rate declining but still in rather alarming rate. Suicide is the leading cause of death for people under 30. 

