===Religion===
[[File:Suwa taisha harumiya13bs3200.jpg|200px|thumb|left|Moriya Shrine in [[Moriya, Kitayama|Moriya]], [[Kitayama Prefecture]]]]
[[File:Kyoto-Kiyomizu Temple-2.JPG|200px|thumb|right|Myouren Temple in [[Ichihara]]]]
Nakama granted full religious freedom based on its constitution since 1907 constitution adapted. Estimated around 60-70% of Nakamaese Population described as Shintoism or follow indigenous religion (excluding Buddhism) however this number may also included non religious figure around Nakama which estimated around 2%-7% of total population. around 20-30% of Nakamaese is Buddhist which also added to the indigenous religion aside with Shintoism which combined both total would be 90% of its population. Nakamaese Shintoism based on its original shintoism in Japan which influenced by Taoism, Confucianism from china as well. Despite of high degree of follower, Only around 5% of its population actually belong to the Shinto organization while the rest 55% of the population is unaffiliated shintoism.
